message: "If you use this programme, its software, or its project-authored data, cite the programme and every relevant upstream source."
title: "Agency Transfer Research Programme"
type: software
version: 0.3.0-draft
date-released: 2026-08-28
authors:
  - family-names: "Guerrero Manchón"
    given-names: "Miguel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/apolmig/agencytransfer"
url: "https://miguelguerrero.eu/agencytransfer/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A maintained research programme on frontier AI, harmful manipulation,
  election security, agency transfer, and concentrated democratic power. It
  integrates four research strands: served-system operationalisation,
  capability measurement, election evidence, and policy intervention. The
  programme preserves the Capability–Deployment–Effect Gap and does not treat
  evidence at one layer as proof of authentic exposure, human effect, agency
  transfer, or electoral consequence at another.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - harmful manipulation
  - election security
  - agency transfer
  - democratic power
  - persuasion
  - agentic systems
  - model evaluation
  - AI governance

